oved.","For any citation with a non-blank snippet, every string formatCitation returns — whatever the source_type or URL validity — starts with '- ' and carries the snippet as a two-space-indented blockquote line ('\\n  > \"<snippet>\"') on its own line, so formatSources output remains a single markdown list and no entry merges into the previous item.","The fallback paths still emit no markdown link: the YouTube fallback contains no '[<title>](' watch/deep-link, and the Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback contains no ']('.","The console.warn message '[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \"<url>\"' is emitted unchanged on both YouTube fallback branches (pinned verbatim by an existing test).","Only one production file changes: app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts; test changes are confined to app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts."],"issue":{"number":49,"title":"fix(export): markdown export drops the transcript snippet when a citation URL cannot be parsed"},"out_of_scope":["Backend, schema, and any new or changed package dependency.","CitationModal.tsx, Message.tsx, ChatArea.tsx, Sidebar.tsx, and any production file other than app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts.","The valid-URL (YouTube '?v=') and valid-lesson_url happy-path return shapes — they are kept as-is and proven by guards AC-4/AC-5, not modified.","formatTimestamp, the export header, and the filename slug.","Changing URL parsing itself (e.g. adding youtu.be/<id> path-ID support): repairing the no-v fallback incidentally improves youtu.be exports, but the parsing logic stays as-is per the issue's scope."],"risks":["REPRO DEFERRED TO RED: no existing command fails on the unchanged tree — the three existing fallback tests were written against the buggy return strings — so the red proof exists only through the new AC-1..AC-3 checkpoints, which must be shown failing (with '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' in a red checkpoint's output) before the fix is applied.","The exact repaired fallback string is not pinned beyond AC-1/AC-2/AC-3 (marker, '(timestamp link unavailable)' plus range, blockquote on its own line); any shape satisfying them while keeping every current case green is acceptable.","En dash (–, U+2013) inside timestamp ranges vs em dash (—, U+2014) before them are easily swapped in assertions or output; both the fixed code and the new tests must use the same characters as the existing source.","vitest only embeds the received string in toMatch/toContain-style assertion failures; a boolean assertion like expect(result.startsWith('- ')).toBe(true) would go red without displaying the expected symptom, so the AC-1/AC-2 red checkpoints should assert on the result string content.","console.warn must be suppressed (or mocked) in the new tests where it fires, matching the existing suite's vi.spyOn(console, 'warn') pattern, so the checkpoints do not pollute output."],"summary":"Repair the three fallback return statements in formatCitation (app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts:32, :46, :53) so every citation entry — the YouTube unparseable-video_url and no-v-param fallbacks and the Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback — keeps the quoted transcript snippet blockquote and the leading '- ' list marker, matching the shape the valid paths already emit; append AC-1..AC-3 acceptance cases to the existing app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts without breaking any current case.","version":"2.0"},"sha256":"f62a2becb08d5c4b757f50c5300450f609b15f59e46dfd79cc3eb76e280622ee","source":"task-contract.json"},"design":{"content":{"ac_mapping":{"AC-1":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-2":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-3":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-4":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-5":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-6":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-7":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"]},"allowed_new_files":[],"context_sha256":"9a98df9989f7f67def256d38c2ec4af494278d7d9e6c51893bcfd2fa235b4dde","contract_sha256":"f62a2becb08d5c4b757f50c5300450f609b15f59e46dfd79cc3eb76e280622ee","data_flows":["Citation -> formatCitation -> markdown list entry string; happy paths: '- [title](url) — <range>\\n  > \"<snippet>\"'; repaired fallbacks: '- <title> (timestamp link unavailable) — <range>\\n  > \"<snippet>\"' (YouTube catch and no-v branches) and '- <title> — <range>\\n  > \"<snippet>\"' (Dynamous empty lesson_url)","formatCitation entries -> formatSources -> '\\n\\n**Sources:**\\n' + entries joined by '\\n' (single markdown list)","messages -> exportConversationAsMarkdown -> Blob via saveAs -> conversation-<slug>-<date>.md download"],"invariants":["Every current case in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts keeps passing; existing cases may be strengthened to pin the repaired fallback shape, but none may be weakened, skipped, or removed.","For any citation with a non-blank snippet, every string formatCitation returns — whatever the source_type or URL validity — starts with '- ' and carries the snippet as a two-space-indented blockquote line ('\\n  > \"<snippet>\"') on its own line, so formatSources output remains a single markdown list and no entry merges into the previous item.","The fallback paths still emit no markdown link: the YouTube fallback contains no '[<title>](' watch/deep-link, and the Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback contains no ']('.","The console.warn message '[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \"<url>\"' is emitted unchanged on both YouTube fallback branches (pinned verbatim by an existing test).","Only one production file changes: app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts; test changes are confined to app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts.","The empty/whitespace/missing-snippet early guard (exportMarkdown.ts:22) keeps returning '' before any URL handling — n